# Copy to .env (or just `export` these in your shell / job script) to
# override where data/results live. None of these are required -- with
# nothing set, everything defaults to ./data and ./results relative to the
# repo root, which is what makes a fresh `git clone` work with zero setup.
#
# Example for running on a cluster with data living elsewhere:
#   export HWML_DATA_DIR=/scratch3/dpappert/CESM2/ML
#   export HWML_RESULTS_DIR=/scratch3/dpappert/CESM2/ML/results

# HWML_DATA_DIR=/path/to/data
# HWML_RESULTS_DIR=/path/to/results
# HWML_SPLITS_DIR=/path/to/data/precomputed_splits
